{"id":"ltc-disclosure-check","title":"The case's nursing-home figures, checked against each home's own report","question":"Do the related-party balances, payments and profits used in the nursing-home case match what each home filed with the State?","finding":"40 of 42 homes agree to the dollar on all three figures (amount owed by related parties, related-party payments on page 10.4, net income); 2 differ: Morton Bakar Center, San Jose Healthcare & Wellness Center. The 42 reports together carry $1,021.5 million owed by related parties and list $71.0 million of related-party transactions.","how":"Each home's latest facsimile report on the State's SIERA site was read table by table. Owed by related parties = receivables from related parties (page 5.1 lines 50 and 160) less payables to related parties (page 5.2 lines 45 and 110). Payments = the 'Total Adjustments' transaction total on page 10.4. Net income = page 8 line 255. Compared with the rows of screen 'ltc-related-balance-check' (nursing_money), which read the State's complete data set.","limits":"Both sources are the same filing, so agreement shows the data set was read correctly, not that the figures are right; the 2025 reports are as submitted and not yet audited. A home that books a related balance as a negative number is shown as a positive amount owed, as in the case.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Nursing home","type":"org"},{"k":"city","t":"City","type":"text"},{"k":"periodEnd","t":"Report ends","type":"text"},{"k":"relatedNet","t":"Owed by related parties (report)","type":"usd"},{"k":"caseRelatedNet","t":"Same, in the case","type":"usd"},{"k":"paidRelated","t":"Related-party transactions (report)","type":"usd"},{"k":"casePaid","t":"Same, in the case","type":"usd"},{"k":"netIncome","t":"Net income (report)","type":"usd"},{"k":"caseNetIncome","t":"Same, in the case","type":"usd"},{"k":"status","t":"Check","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"home":"Morton Bakar Center","city":"Hayward","periodEnd":"06/3